504839eb (3404 1794311854366 "import-git" (("4gm4c2jr" . 3240) ("w5vbequy" . 14982)) (put ((kind . decision) (slot . "import") (from . "b026c601c650e409dede9037d073d3c902e21fc9") (to . "de6212cdec627f0a15109c60dde0e937c33182e7") (tag . "import-sb8") (status . "pending") (src . "write --expect: a rebase names the draft version it judged\ndaemon: a lock that cannot be taken is answered by the table, not as busy\ntest: the load census lists draft-changed-refusal's obtain-state\nlog: every entry into a load traces log-open, in open-load itself\nstore: a tracked request beside an unreadable entry is refused by the table\ncore: a forwarded request carries THEOURGIA_WRITER when the command line names no writer\ncode-project: capture-import keeps its intents newest first, its ids in a table\ntest: the verb registry's base takes write's new entry\ndaemon: a publish refused at the start is reported as the start's refusal\ndatum-project: every import warning names its file\nsplit-suggest: nothing is written beside the input; the answer carries the review text\ntest: launch-self's census guard reads a retry as a reading\nclient: a socket directory that cannot be searched is refused by name\neval: a value is held to the limit by its written text; K14's helper reads the whole answer\ntest: the handler census pins the failure paths the batch changed\ntest: store-in-git stops G1's daemon through the checked signal helpers\ntest: the guard's expect file lists trace lines; describe and log-open\ntest: the guard expect file emptied after the landing it listed\ntest: GUARD-3 takes a listed trace line exactly as often as it is listed\ntest: the guard expect file emptied after the landing it listed\n") (parent . root) (ord . 668))))
